  "limitations": "Legacy double-precision method, not a modern uniform-asymptotic implementation. Shape 1e-5..1000 and x 0..10000; extreme tails can underflow and subtraction can lose relative tail accuracy. This is a special-function primitive, not a fitted distribution, quantile solver or statistical significance recommendation. No arbitrary precision or blanket digit guarantee.",
  "port_notes": "Ports the v0.15.1 C igam.c algorithm (source identifies Cephes April 1987), including branch selection, MAXLOG guard, fraction renormalization by 2^52 and series convergence at MACHEP=2^-53. Python math.lgamma substitutes for the separate Cephes lgam implementation; iteration caps are explicit new safety bounds. The old source carries its original copyright but only a platform include and algorithm body are redistributed as compilable evidence; a nonlegal postal-contact line is omitted. Full SciPy BSD text and the separately pinned explicit Cephes BSD author-permission block are preserved. No claim of bit-identical full-Cephes behavior.",
